class Solution {
    public int getLength(ListNode head) {

        // Counter to store the number of nodes
        int count = 0;

        // Start traversal from the head
        ListNode current = head;

        // Traverse until the end of the linked list
        while (current != null) {

            // Count the current node
            count++;

            // Move to the next node
            current = current.next;
        }

        // Return the total number of nodes
        return count;
    }
}

Quick explanation

Start from head and traverse every node using current = current.next. For every node visited, increment count. When current becomes null, the traversal is complete, so return count.

Time: O(n) — every node is visited once.
Auxiliary Space: O(1) — only count and current are used.
